# Pipeline providers

Business logic calls ports. Vendor SDKs stay in `providers/`.

## Translation

`translate(text, source_language, target_language)` — natural narration in the **target** language, not word-for-word. Map provider language codes **inside** the adapter (`zh` → `zho` for NLLB). `source_language` may be `auto` if the provider/detector supports it.

```python
# BAD
if provider == "nllb":
    ...
if source_language == "zh":
    ...

# GOOD
await translation_provider.translate(text, source_language, target_language)
```

## Narration

Do not send raw translation to TTS. A dedicated narration stage may normalize punctuation, pauses, dialogue, numbers, abbreviations, and sentence boundaries **without changing meaning**.

## TTS

`synthesize(text, language, voice, settings)`. Voice must be compatible with `target_language`. Voices are listed by the provider and chosen by the user (or config default **for that language**), never a single global Vietnamese (or any) voice.

Edge TTS is the **MVP adapter**, not the domain model. Piper, XTTS, Chatterbox, ElevenLabs, Azure, Google must plug in without changing domain/application orchestration.

## Audio

Providers do not share codec/rate/channels. Normalize with FFmpeg **before** merge. Incremental/file-based processing; do not load the whole story audio into memory. See security rule for subprocess invocation.
